WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.060
He created a body that was to become the gold
standard for muscular development.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:09.740
He would use it achieve one goal after another,
rising to the very pinnacle of, not one, but

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:10.950
three careers.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.990
Yet, from the very start Arnold Schwarzenegger
had the odds stacked against him...

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:20.020
He was dismissed, ridiculed and parodied mercilessly.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.860
What people failed to realize was that Arnold’s
strongest muscle was, not his bicep, but his

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.060
brain.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.820
With it he orchestrated career moves that
took him to the very top.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:36.130
In this Biographics video, we uncover the
unlikely rags to riches story of the one and

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.770
only Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:42.950
“For me life is continuously being hungry.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:57.030
The meaning of life is not simply to exist,
to survive, but to move ahead, to go up, to

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.250
achieve, to conquer.”

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.739
Early Life

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:04.750
Arnold Alois Schwarzenegger was born in the
tiny Austrian village of Thal, near Graz on

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.900
July 30th 1947.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.630
His father, Gustav was the local police chief.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.420
Arnold and his older brother, Meinhard, grew
up under the tough discipline of a man who

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.970
was used to being obeyed.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.880
Arnold’s early years were very regimented.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.080
He’d be up at six, and then off to get milk
from the farm next door.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.380
Then he would have to do a set of physical
exercises that his father had written out

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.920
for him – earning his breakfast by doing
a certain number of sit ups.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.700
In the afternoon, after he’d finished his
homework and chores, his father made Arnold

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.380
and Meinhard practice soccer no matter how
bad the weather was.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.970
If they messed up on a play, they got yelled
at…

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.979
Gustav himself had been a champion ice curler
in his younger years and he pushed his sons

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:44.690
to excel physically.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.850
With his father’s pushing, Arnold first
got into organized competitive sports at the

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.850
age of ten.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.299
He played soccer passionately for almost five
years.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:56.049
When he was fifteen, Arnold’s soccer coach
decided that lifting weights for an hour once

00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:00.439
a week would be a good way for his players
to stay in shape, so he took them for a visit

00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:02.090
to the local gym.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.860
That day would change Arnold’s life.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:11.780
He was mesmerized by the size of the bodybuilders
who stalked the gym, waging war with the steel

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.780
weights.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.390
Arnold would later record his feelings in
his 1977 autobiography Arnold: The Education

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:18.390
of a Bodybuilder . . .

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.580
There it was before me – my life, the answer
I’d been seeking.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.580
It clicked.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.120
It was something I suddenly just seemed to
reach out and find, as if I’d been crossing

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.900
a suspended bridge and finally stepped off
onto solid ground.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.680
Arnold embraced weight lifting.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.730
He soon discovered that he had an amazing
ability to build muscle.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.620
Within two years he had already overtaken
most of the other trainers at the gym in Graz

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.910
where he worked out religiously.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.530
He also trained harder than anyone else.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:49.360
One Sunday, discovering that the gym was closed,
he smashed the window to get in so that he

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.090
could get in his workout.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:56.800
Arnold’s father was less than impressed
with his son’s new found obsession.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.680
Bodybuilding was very much a fringe sport
in Austria at that time, with those who partook

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.069
of it being look down upon and considered
in some way defective.

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:09.690
When it was discovered that Arnold had pictures
of half naked men with bulging muscles on

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:14.910
his bedroom wall, a psychiatrist was called
in to ‘save’ Arnold from himself.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:19.770
The psychiatrist assured his parents that
this was a phase that Arnold would grow out

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:20.770
of.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.989
Oh, how wrong he was.

00:03:23.989 --> 00:03:27.879
By the age of seventeen Arnold had already
realized that bodybuilding was going to be

00:03:27.879 --> 00:03:30.550
his vehicle to worldwide fame.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:34.489
He had spent many Saturday afternoons down
at the local movie theater watching bodybuilders

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:39.120
turned actors such as Steve Reeves and, his
personal favorite, Reg Park - he watched them

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.620
on screen playing Hercules and other mythic
heroes.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:46.370
They had used bodybuilding to create careers
as movie stars.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:52.690
And that was exactly what he would do – only
he would be bigger and better than any of

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:55.070
them...

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:59.830
Army Life

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:09.000
Arnold entered the Austrian army in 1965 to
fulfill his obligatory one year of service.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.950
By now he’d built his body to 200 pounds
of Herculean muscle.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.239
He was assigned as a driver in a tank unit.

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:20.259
Shortly after he was inducted, Arnold received
an invitation to compete in the junior division

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:23.150
of the Mr. Europe contest in Stuttgart, Germany.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.349
But he was in the middle of basic training...

00:04:25.349 --> 00:04:28.809
No soldier was allowed to leave the base for
any reason.

00:04:28.809 --> 00:04:33.809
But Arnold knew that his destiny was tied
with winning this contest, so he decided to

00:04:33.809 --> 00:04:35.789
go AWOL in order to compete.

00:04:35.789 --> 00:04:39.770
He crawled over the wall, taking only the
clothes he was wearing and barely enough money

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.009
to buy a third class ticket to Germany.

00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:45.270
When he finally arrived at the competition,
he had to borrow someone else’s posing trunks

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.949
and tanning oil.

00:04:46.949 --> 00:04:52.289
Still his muscles were undeniable and that
night he was announced Junior Mr. Europe.

00:04:52.289 --> 00:04:54.029
At first the army was not impressed.

00:04:54.029 --> 00:04:59.099
He was put in jail for seven days with only
a blanket on a cold stone bench and almost

00:04:59.099 --> 00:05:00.099
no food.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:04.439
But within a few days the news of his victory
had spread and the top brass decided that

00:05:04.439 --> 00:05:06.300
the title added prestige to the army.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:10.080
When he returned to the ranks, he was held
up as a sort of ideal, with his drill instructor

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.080
telling the troops . . .

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.699
“You have to fight for your fatherland.

00:05:12.699 --> 00:05:13.800
You have to take courage.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:17.180
Look at what Schwarzenegger did just to win
this title.”

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.869
Following his stint in the army, Arnold took
a job as a gym instructor at a Health Club

00:05:20.869 --> 00:05:22.319
in Munich, Germany.

00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:27.580
This presented him with the ideal opportunity
to train for the 1966 Mr. Europe competition.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:32.219
This was the next step in his master plan
to become the best built man on the planet.

00:05:32.219 --> 00:05:38.030
He trained twice a day, working like a man
possessed in order to forge the winning physique.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:41.749
By the time he arrived in Stuttgart for the
Mr. Europe contest, people were anxious to

00:05:41.749 --> 00:05:46.690
get a look at this “monster from Munich”
who they’d heard rumors about.

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:51.449
All of the attention infused Arnold with a
great deal of confidence, and he already felt

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:52.449
like the winner.

00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:56.080
Arnold’s win that day was so emphatic that
the judges offered to pay his way to the upcoming

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.499
Mr. Universe contest.

00:05:57.499 --> 00:06:02.719
He arrived in London, knowing almost no English,
but as soon as he stepped out of his cab,

00:06:02.719 --> 00:06:04.469
people began mobbing him.

00:06:04.469 --> 00:06:09.129
They had all been waiting for him – the
first bodybuilder in Europe with 20-inch arms.

00:06:09.129 --> 00:06:11.330
Still, he didn’t win that day.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:17.119
The American had a more complete, defined
physique and he forced Arnold to accept second

00:06:17.119 --> 00:06:18.179
place.

00:06:18.179 --> 00:06:21.039
Arnold returned to Munich and threw himself
back into his training.

00:06:21.039 --> 00:06:27.669
He shut everything out of his mind and concentrated
on only one thing – winning the 1967 Mr.

00:06:27.669 --> 00:06:28.669
Universe.

00:06:28.669 --> 00:06:35.300
Sure enough, on September 23rd, 1967 Arnold
Schwarzenegger became, at 20 years of age,

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.899
the youngest Mr. Universe in history.

00:06:37.899 --> 00:06:42.849
A year later an even more massive Arnold returned
to London to claim the Professional Mr. Universe

00:06:42.849 --> 00:06:43.849
title.

00:06:43.849 --> 00:06:47.099
Following that victory, Arnold received the
phone call that would prove to be the next

00:06:47.099 --> 00:06:49.069
great signpost to his future.

00:06:49.069 --> 00:06:53.789
On the other end of the line was Joe Weider,
bodybuilding guru and publisher of Muscle

00:06:53.789 --> 00:06:54.959
Builder Magazine.

00:06:54.959 --> 00:06:59.780
Weider invited Arnold to compete in the IFBB
Mr. Universe in Miami, and then come to train

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:08.789
in California and work for him.

00:07:08.789 --> 00:07:12.629
America

00:07:12.629 --> 00:07:18.460
Arnold arrived in America in September, 1968,
with a gym bag, twenty US dollars and virtually

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.460
no English.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.770
He settled into a small apartment in Venice
Beach and was given a small stipend by Weider

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.250
in exchange for the rights to use his image
in magazines.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:31.439
Arnold’s plan was to stay in the USA for
one year, absorb their training strategies

00:07:31.439 --> 00:07:34.379
and then use them to beat the Americans at
their own game.

00:07:34.379 --> 00:07:38.770
Arnold began training at a small gym at Venice
Beach, Los Angeles called Gold’s Gym.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:43.119
He rubbed shoulders with all the top American
bodybuilders but quickly established himself

00:07:43.119 --> 00:07:44.740
as the leader of the pack...

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:49.990
In 1970, Arnold won the coveted triple crown
of bodybuilding: claiming the Mr. Universe,

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.639
Mr. World, and the Mr. Olympia titles.

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:56.619
He was now the undisputed king of bodybuilding.

00:07:56.619 --> 00:08:02.659
Arnold went on to win 6 consecutive Mr. Olympia
titles as he completely dominated the sport...

00:08:02.659 --> 00:08:07.999
Now he was ready to implement phase two of
his master plan.

00:08:07.999 --> 00:08:10.439
Acting

00:08:10.439 --> 00:08:20.969
In 1970, Joe Weider got a call from a film
production company looking for a bodybuilder

00:08:20.969 --> 00:08:23.129
to play Hercules in a low budget film.

00:08:23.129 --> 00:08:27.319
Weider immediately thought of Arnold, telling
the producer that Arnie had been a Shakespearean

00:08:27.319 --> 00:08:29.300
actor back in Europe.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.919
They signed him up immediately.

00:08:30.919 --> 00:08:32.849
The result was Hercules Goes to New York.

00:08:32.849 --> 00:08:36.599
It was to be Arnold’s first, and most forgettable
film.

00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:40.659
His credit reads ‘Arnold Strong’ and his
thick Austrian accent was dubbed over.

00:08:40.659 --> 00:08:46.279
Still, he got paid $10,000 which he invested
into California real estate.

00:08:46.279 --> 00:08:49.210
His next paycheck took some time coming...

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.980
Arnold found Hollywood less receptive than
he had hoped.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:55.990
Several agents told him that he had everything
going against him – he had a long name which

00:08:55.990 --> 00:09:01.050
was difficult to pronounce, a strange accent
and, to top it off, an ‘unusual build which

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.620
will never make it into films.’

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:05.960
For Arnold, this was the very motivation that
he needed.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:10.069
Back in Austria he had been told that he could
never become a champion bodybuilder and yet

00:09:10.069 --> 00:09:12.350
that is exactly what he had become.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:16.649
Now he would reinvent himself through the
same sheer hard work and dedication that he

00:09:16.649 --> 00:09:21.120
had learnt in the gym in order to become the
highest paid movie star on the planet.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.140
He would make the agents eat their words…

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.720
Arnold began acting lessons in 1974.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:30.710
He won a supporting role in the Bob Raffelson
movie Stay Hungry.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:35.589
He played a bodybuilder named Joe Santo, so
it hardly stretched his acting talents.

00:09:35.589 --> 00:09:38.790
Still he was determined to make an impression.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:39.930
Make an impression he did.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.050
He won the Golden Globe for best newcomer.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:45.520
Then, in 1977 the documentary Pumping Iron
opened in theaters.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:50.610
The film chronicled Arnold’s victory in
the 1975 Mr. Olympia over Lou Ferrigno - the

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.030
future Incredible Hulk.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:56.579
As his charming, confident self, Arnold’s
on-screen charisma was impossible to resist.

00:09:56.579 --> 00:10:00.160
Pumping Iron led to small roles in The Villain
and The Jayne Mansfield Story..

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.120
Businessman

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:16.589
By now, Arnold was already a successful businessman,
combining real estate investments, a best

00:10:16.589 --> 00:10:19.730
selling biography, and bodybuilding training
courses.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:22.550
This meant that he could afford to wait for
just the right film project.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.920
He filled his time with public appearances
and social functions.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:29.360
One such function was the Robert F. Kennedy
Tennis Tournament in Hyannisport.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:34.560
There he caught the eye of a beautiful dark
haired girl by the name of Maria Shriver.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:39.519
She was the daughter of Sargent and Eunice
Kennedy Shriver and the niece of John Fitzgerald

00:10:39.519 --> 00:10:40.519
Kennedy.

00:10:40.519 --> 00:10:42.699
Arnold and Maria fell in love at first sight.

00:10:42.699 --> 00:10:46.870
The Shrivers were great philanthropists and
through them Arnold was introduced to the

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:50.560
Special Olympics, which he has been passionately
involved with ever since.

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:54.300
In 1979, Arnold began a career as a CBS sports
commentator.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:58.459
He also graduated from the University of Wisconsin
with a business degree.

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:03.029
A year later, he stunned the bodybuilding
world with his comeback at the Mr. Olympia

00:11:03.029 --> 00:11:04.780
competition in Australia.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:10.649
There he captured his 7th title, cementing
his legendary status as the greatest bodybuilder

00:11:10.649 --> 00:11:11.720
of all time.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:14.060
Arnold’s comeback, however, wasn’t without
controversy.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:18.449
He went to Australia in the role of a TV reporter,
only signing his name on the competitor register

00:11:18.449 --> 00:11:19.899
at the last minute.

00:11:19.899 --> 00:11:23.759
He was also good friends with head judge,
bodybuilding legend Bill Pearl.

00:11:23.759 --> 00:11:27.899
The general consensus was that the Arnold
on stage was a mere shadow of his former self.

00:11:27.899 --> 00:11:31.050
His victory was, for the first time, greeted
by boo’s.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:41.220
Still, his 7th Mr. Olympia title was on the
books.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.100
Breakthrough

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:49.160
The great shape that Arnold had got into for
the 1980 Mr. Olympia propelled him into his

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.699
breakthrough role as Conan the Barbarian.

00:11:51.699 --> 00:11:56.079
After spending a year in training working
on his speech and learning how to use iron

00:11:56.079 --> 00:12:01.629
broadswords, he headed of to Yugoslavia and
Spain for a grueling 6-month shoot.

00:12:01.629 --> 00:12:05.300
Conan the Barbarian raked in more than $100
million at the box office.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:10.389
Together with its sequel, Conan the Destroyer,
it firmly embedded the name Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:12:10.389 --> 00:12:12.170
into movie goes consciousnesses.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:17.180
Following his success with the Conan movies,
Arnold was offered a low budget movie by first

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.920
time director and screenwriter James Cameron.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.379
This would prove to be his most iconic role.

00:12:23.379 --> 00:12:27.499
In The Terminator, Arnold plays a cyborg sent
back in time to kill the mother of the man

00:12:27.499 --> 00:12:29.800
who will save humankind from destruction.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.820
The role, it was made for Arnold.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:35.390
His accent and his body – the very things
that the agents had said would work against

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:37.850
him – were perfect to play the part of the
T-1000.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:44.060
The Terminator was a worldwide smash, firmly
establishing Arnold as the next great action

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.060
star.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:47.900
By 1985, he had already been named International
Star of the Year.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:53.940
On April 26th, 1986 Arnold, a staunch Republican,
and Maria Shriver, a member of Democratic

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.050
royalty, were married.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:13:01.339
The honeymoon was barely over before Arnold
flew to Mexico to film his latest action blockbuster,

00:13:01.339 --> 00:13:02.339
Predator.

00:13:02.339 --> 00:13:05.459
This movie again won him the title of action
star of the year.

00:13:05.459 --> 00:13:09.010
After a string of action films – Commando,
Raw Deal, Predator and The Running Man – the

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:15.589
forward thinking Arnold was ready for a new
challenge – and that, was comedy.

00:13:15.589 --> 00:13:18.990
Few were willing to take a gamble on Arnold
the comic actor.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:23.879
But one who was was director Ivan Reitman,
who created a special vehicle for Arnold.

00:13:23.879 --> 00:13:26.060
That vehicle was called Twins…

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:31.040
The irresistible chemistry of Schwarzenegger
and Danny DeVito made Twins an immediate hit.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:35.660
Two years later, Arnold again teamed with
Reitman for Kindergarten Cop, another comedy

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.660
success.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:40.690
A large part of the success of these films
is Arnold’s ability to laugh at himself.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:43.730
Arnold always got the joke, which was very
endearing to fans.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:47.839
Over and above that, Arnold was a gifted comedian,
which anybody whose seen Pumping Iron will

00:13:47.839 --> 00:13:48.839
know.

00:13:48.839 --> 00:13:51.910
One person who noticed Arnold’s abilities
on Kindergarten Cop – especially his rapport

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:53.980
with children – was President George Bush.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:59.029
Bush appointed Arnold as the Chairman of the
Presidents’ Council on Physical Fitness.

00:13:59.029 --> 00:14:04.829
This could have been a largely symbolic role,
but Arnold threw himself into it with relish,

00:14:04.829 --> 00:14:07.980
visiting every state to promote the fitness
lifestyle.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:13.089
The movie winning streak continued for Arnold
– with Total Recall, and Terminator 2.

00:14:13.089 --> 00:14:17.670
This sequel cost $102 million, making it the
most expensive film to that date.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:24.900
It returned $519.8 million, with Arnie pocketing
a cool $15 million.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:30.550
Arnold’s next big movie outing was Last
Action Hero, a hundred-million dollar extravaganza

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.170
which seemed like a sure thing.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:35.959
But the film was a box office bomb, and a
critical flop.

00:14:35.959 --> 00:14:40.310
Hollywood was quick to tear Arnie down, claiming
that his time in the limelight was over.

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:43.329
But Schwarzenegger had other ideas.

00:14:43.329 --> 00:14:47.329
He bounced back from defeat with the same
focused determination as in his bodybuilding

00:14:47.329 --> 00:14:48.329
days.

00:14:48.329 --> 00:14:51.590
He reteamed with James Cameron for the action-back
James Bond spoof True Lies.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:15:02.440
The movie was a smash and Arnold was back
on top.

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:07.970
Governorship

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:11.800
In the mid-1990’s Arnold began focusing
on giving back to the country that had given

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.800
him so much.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:16.720
He became an organizer and sponsor of the
Annual Inner City Games.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.829
He was also very involved in the After School
Care program.

00:15:19.829 --> 00:15:25.480
In 2003, during an appearance on the Jay Leno
show, Arnold announced his candidacy for Governor

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.740
of California.

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:30.899
This was following the recall of Governor
Gray Davis, sparked by the California electricity

00:15:30.899 --> 00:15:31.899
crisis.

00:15:31.899 --> 00:15:36.129
Arnold ran an energetic campaign, despite
a smear campaign organized by the LA Times.

00:15:36.129 --> 00:15:40.740
A number of women claimed that, over the years,
Arnold had molested them, while others claimed

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.189
to have had affairs with him.

00:15:42.189 --> 00:15:46.750
Still, Arnold was able to rise above this
with his unique mix of charm, intelligence

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:47.750
and wit.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:51.040
On one occasion, someone in a crowd threw
an egg which splattered on Arnie’s jacket.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:55.029
He immediately whipped the jacket off, threw
it over his shoulder and called out to the

00:15:55.029 --> 00:15:57.149
thrower, ‘Hey, I ordered bacon with those
eggs!’

00:15:57.149 --> 00:16:01.829
He easily won the Governorship and immediately
set about cleaning house at Sacramento.

00:16:01.829 --> 00:16:04.899
Bringing his own unique style to the position
he would constantly refer to his Democratic

00:16:04.899 --> 00:16:06.670
opposition as ‘girlie men.’

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:11.660
Arnold’s first term was marked by such early
victories as repealing a vehicle license increase

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:14.610
and stopping illegals from getting driver's
licenses.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:18.860
But then powerful state unions began to oppose
his initiatives and four ballot measures he

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:22.899
sponsored in a special election in 2005 were
defeated.

00:16:22.899 --> 00:16:27.699
Despite this, Arnold was re-elected Governor
in 2006 with 56% of the vote.

00:16:27.699 --> 00:16:30.730
On his second term he put a lot of effort
in environmental issues.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:36.360
In 2006 he signed the Global Warming Solutions
Act, making California the first state to

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.870
put a cap on greenhouse gas emissions.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:42.829
Arnold’s second term as Governor came to
an end in January, 2011.

00:16:42.829 --> 00:16:47.250
A few months later the LA Times ran a cover
story reporting that Arnold had fathered a

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:51.149
child fourteen years previously with the family’s
long time maid.

00:16:51.149 --> 00:16:56.390
As a direct result of this revelation Arnold
and Maria ended their 25-year marriage.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:17:07.900
She and their four children moved out of the
family home in Brentwood.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.549
Post-Governorship

00:17:09.549 --> 00:17:14.199
Arnold’s post Governorship movie career
has seen him feature in such action flicks

00:17:14.199 --> 00:17:19.370
as The Expendables 2 &amp; 3, Escape Plan, Sabotage
and the fifth instalment of Terminator in

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.610
which he battles his younger self.

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:24.560
Arnold has continued to maintain strong ties
to the bodybuilding world.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:28.940
Following his retirement from the sport in
1975, he promoted the Mr. Olympia competition.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:34.510
Then, in 1989, he and long time partner Jim
Lorimer started the Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:39.770
Classic, which is now the second biggest Pro
Bodybuilding Show, behind the Mr. Olympia.

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:44.830
Arnold credits all of his success to the self
discipline, drive and focus that he learnt

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.980
from his bodybuilding career.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:50.130
In recent times, Arnold has been involved
in a Social Media feud with President Donald

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.720
Trump, in the wake of Arnie’s replacing
Trump on Celebrity Apprentice.

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:57.350
Trump blamed Arnold for the show’s dismal
ratings, with Arnold offering the Commander-in-Chief

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.850
some timely advice on how to run the country.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:05.409
Arnold, a staunch Republican, refused to vote
for Trump in the 2016 presidential election,

00:18:05.409 --> 00:18:09.640
the first time he had not supported the Republican
candidate since becoming a US citizen.

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:13.690
Although it’s one battle that we’d all
love to see, Arnold cannot challenge The Donald

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:17.350
for the top job as he wasn’t born in the
United States, even though he did become a

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:19.230
citizen in 1983.

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:21.710
Arnold still lives the fitness lifestyle.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:48.370
Having just celebrated his 70th birthday,
he works out every day.

